## Goal
Show how the six samples relate to one another in gene-expression space, with a principal component analysis of the gene-level counts, drawn as a single plot with samples coloured by treated versus untreated.

## Inputs
Artifact types resolve through each sub-stage's OUTPUTS.tsv at execution time; the paths
below are what they resolve to today.

| Artifact type | Resolved from | Path |
|---|---|---|
| `counts_gene` | `02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper` (native) | `02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv` |

The `condition` labels (untreated: A1-A3, treated: B1-B3) come from the stage 01 design table,
`01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk_design.csv`, read as a project file rather than an artifact.

## Method
Environment: `gars-bio` (python3 with numpy, pandas, matplotlib). Script: `scripts/sample_pca.py`.
Inputs are read-only.

1. Read the `counts_gene` matrix (genes x samples; `gene_id` and `gene_name` are identifiers, the
   other six columns are samples A1-A3, B1-B3). Read the design table and match samples by
   `sample_id`; stop with an error if the two sample sets differ.
2. Drop genes with zero counts in every sample, then transform with log2(count + 1). The matrix is
   already length-scaled, so no further size-factor normalisation is applied.
3. Keep the 500 genes with the highest variance across samples (a fixed choice, stated here so it
   is not tuned after seeing the plot).
4. Centre each gene across samples; do not scale to unit variance. Run PCA by SVD
   (`numpy.linalg.svd`) on the samples x genes matrix.
5. Plot PC1 (x) against PC2 (y), one point per sample, coloured by `condition` (treated vs
   untreated; two colour-blind-safe colours, with a legend), each point labelled with its sample
   ID, axes labelled with percent variance explained. Save as PNG at 300 dpi.
6. Print the variance explained by each PC to the job log. No other statistics are computed.

## Outputs
Types come from the closed vocabulary in _references/artifact_types.md.

| File | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `results/sample_pca.png` | `figure` | PC1 vs PC2 of the six samples, coloured treated / untreated, axes labelled with percent variance explained |

## Execution
Runs: batch
Expected wall time: under a minute (six samples, one small matrix). Output: one PNG, well under
1 MB. Submitted through the executor door; no login-node execution was requested.
